 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "gas hob keeps clickin on its own since i cleand it, stops then starts agen. drivin me mad. pls help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That rapid clicking is the ignition system trying to light a burner that isn't lighting properly. Since this started after cleaning, the most likely cause is that water or detergent has gotten under the burner cap or onto the spark electrode, or the cap hasn't been seated perfectly flat again. Please turn off the gas and unplug the hob if you can. Lift off each burner cap (the metal ring) and the small crown piece in the middle. Check if they are completely dry and sitting square. If any look wet or dirty, wipe them thoroughly with a dry cloth and reseat them firmly. Once that's done, try lighting one burner normally. Does it light immediately without clicking repeatedly?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok i took the caps off n i did slosh loads of water about. one cap was a bit wonky so i put it back right. i unplugged the hob under the sink for the afternoon and its stopped clickin. no gas smell"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news. The clicking was most likely caused by the water and detergent getting under the burner cap, creating a short circuit for the spark. Since it has stopped now, you can plug the hob back in and use it as normal. To stop this happening again, just make sure to dry the burner caps and bases thoroughly after cleaning before putting them back on. If the clicking ever starts up again, unplug the hob for an hour or two to let any internal moisture evaporate."
  }
 ],
